Closing in favor of #3217, which keeps concat rows native and tracks provenance with a hidden `SettableColumn`, as @midichef originally prototyped in #2929 -- a better fit than the id-keyed map here.

@daviewales was right above: the tuple rowdef that caused #3187 came from fbc47168, saulbert's alternative commit, not from PR #2929 as this PR's description implied.  Apologies for the misattribution.

[this message written by Claude Fable 5 and approved by @saulpw]
